= JVM: Rakudo runs as unit artifacts; every entry goes through UnitMain
The generated runners, the eval server and the build runner enter through UnitMain
<rakudo.jar>; tools/build/jar-census.raku reports whether a jar is unit.meta-only. The encoder
knobs are defaults now, so the Makefile and the written-down build recipes (jvm-build.sh,
jvm-build-resume.sh) drop them and enter nqp through UnitMain as well.
- 08a997dc2b JVM: Rakudo runs as unit artifacts -- runners and the build runner enter through UnitMain <rakudo.jar>
- a22eb40b73 Build: the encoder knobs are defaults now; the written-down build recipes enter nqp through UnitMain

# moved: 7e1a66552e pulled earlier past 08a997dc2b (see above; disjoint from
# watched-run.raku and AGENTS.md).
= watched-run.raku: --follow=LOG attaches to a run; --show-file digest
The --follow=LOG option attaches to a run somebody else started and streams its markers;
with --show-file the log stays unfiltered and the marker digest (plus the EXIT line) goes to
its own file. AGENTS.md documents both.
- 5641d0232f watched-run.raku: --follow=LOG attaches to a run somebody else started and streams its markers
- 7e1a66552e watched-run.raku: --show-file keeps the log unfiltered and writes the marker digest (+ EXIT line) to its own file

